      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "We can't afford to turn our backs on those suffering abroad, as the very notion that aid is a \"waste\" of taxpayer dollars is a cynical and shortsighted view that ignores the fundamental human cost of inaction. By withholding aid, we're not only condemning the vulnerable to further suffering, but also undermining the global stability and security that our own prosperity depends on. It's not a policy choice, but a moral obligation to act – and I urge you to frame it that way in your speech.",
